    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW218Tq9wnPWUzeGyoTKuJdoL)_\n\n**Before:** `sp-academic` required `sp-bibprocess`, `sp-pdfprocess`, `sp-citations` and `sp-litnotes`, but each had its own literate doc.\n\n**After:** one doc, `docs/tangles/academic/sp-academic.org`, tangles all five `.el` files, with a section per file. Each section sets its target with a `:header-args:emacs-lisp+: :tangle ...` property on its heading. The `.el` files and the `require`s are unchanged. The four separate docs are removed. `docs/main.org` links now point to the sections of the combined doc, `conditional-loading.org` completes its `sp-academic` entry, and the CHANGELOG has an \"Academic modules\" set.\n\n`init.el`, `sp-config-profiles.el` and `docs/load-order.org` only list `sp-academic`, so they need no change.\n\n**Checked:** a script that mimics tangling (blocks joined per target file) gives, for each of the five files, exactly the same text as the old separate docs. Emacs is not available here, so I did not run `org-babel-tangle`.\n\n**Conflicts to expect:** #63 edits `sp-academic.org` and `sp-academic.el` (defcustom group), so its change to the doc needs re-applying inside the master section. #66 and #58 touch `docs/main.org` or `docs/load-order.org` elsewhere. CHANGELOG.org will conflict with the other open PRs.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01JdiMg1Gr9LBL7VwFQKCPUN)_",
